transparency and authorization  mechanisms for experts that was  announced earlier this week  we have the pleasure to have here with  us today evp domskins  and commissioner kiriakides this  press conference will be followed by a  technical briefing so the press  conference  will be short and we will be able to  provide you  more details during the technical  briefing so please i give the whole  floor first to the evp  uh good afternoon ladies and gentlemen  uh today  the commission has adopted an  implementing regulation  uh making the export of certain products  subject to an  export authorization regulation concerns  transparency and export of code 19  vaccines  the protection and safety of our  citizens is a priority  and the challenges we now face left us  with no  other choice but to act vaccines are key  to the recovery  and to bringing the pandemic under  control  and delivering these vaccines to our  citizens  is the most critical task right now  this is a race against the clock we  cannot lose time  because of vaccines not being delivered  on agreed schedule  to achieve this we need to ensure that  all advanced purchase agreements  for vaccines made by the european union  and are honored  we paid these companies to increase  production and now we expect them  to deliver today's measure has been  adopted with the utmost urgency  the aim is to provide us immediately  with full transparency transparency that  until now has been lacking and what  europeans  expect and if needed it also will  provide  us with a tool to ensure vaccine  deliveries  the commission has adopted a strictly  targeted measure that will allow us to  gather accurate information about the  production of vaccines  and where manufacturers intend to ship  them  the measure is time limited and  specifically applies  to those code 19 vaccines that were  agreed by advanced purchase  agreements the measure is intended to  run  until the end of march we have been very  mindful of  fully honoring 